Z||000000||STEVEN BURTON||11-16-1999||09:33 PM||||MY TEMPETURE GUAGE IS FLUXUATING.<BR>I JUST GOT MY COOLANT SYSTEM FLUSHED BEFORE IT STARTED DOING THIS.IT GOES FROM 110 TO 220+ AND BACK DOWN AGAIN.I DIDENT SEE ANY COOLANT LOSS BUT I FOUND A SMALL CRACK IN THE TOP PART OF MY OVERFLOW TANK. COULD THIS CAUSE THE PROBLEM. <BR>ANY HELP WOULD BE GREATLY APPRECIATED.. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||11-16-1999||10:12 PM||||I'd say if started right after you flushed the system, that you probobly still have air in the system.  Did you bleed it correctly? Here is the link  for properly bleeding your cooling system. Click "Cooling System", then "Beeding the cooling system".  <A HREF="http://www.surf.to/FIERO_OSG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.surf.to/FIERO_OSG</A> <P>The coolant resovoir only holds the "extra" coolant, it should be sealed from the system until pressure gets too high, so I would rule that one out. Make sure it is bled properly first.<P>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-16-1999).]<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-16-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||11-17-1999||12:32 AM||||You have air in the system and it needs burped, but the recovery tank should be replaced too, if it has a crack.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||11-17-1999||04:03 AM||||Is the gauge surging over to 220 really fast or is it just going there when you are sitting in traffic? If it is going there very slowly than thats normal. The engine heats up, the fan turns on it goes back to around 180. If not than you might have an air pocket.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||11-17-1999||09:08 AM||||Recovery tanks are $13 at the Fiero Store. I don't know what GM would want, but I assume the Fiero Store is cheaper.||||reg||1
